# ===========================================================================
# .gitignore - repository-wide ignore policy for the blog platform
#
# Two tiers live in this monorepo, so this file must cover both:
#   backend/    FastAPI service on Python 3.14.7  (byte-code, venvs, caches)
#   frontend/   Next.js 16 app on Node.js 24.19.0 (modules, build output)
#
# Restored after being deleted at commit f8b72d8, which removed 207 lines of
# GitHub's standard Python template. This is deliberately NOT a byte-for-byte
# restoration: several of that template's directory patterns were unanchored
# and silently untrack real source in this repository. Every such pattern is
# anchored or tier-scoped below - see section 2 for the specific hazard.
#
# Two invariants this file exists to guarantee. Verify both with
# `git check-ignore -v <path>` before changing anything here; do not eyeball
# it, because the failure mode of a bad pattern is invisible at commit time.
#
#   1. No secret is committable.  `.env` and every local variant is ignored,
#      while `.env.example` - the documented configuration contract - stays
#      tracked. The pairing IS the design: ignore both and developers have no
#      contract; ignore neither and a real credential gets committed.
#   2. Dependencies stay reproducible.  Every pin artefact remains trackable:
#      backend/requirements.txt, backend/requirements-dev.txt,
#      backend/pyproject.toml, backend/.python-version, frontend/package.json,
#      frontend/package-lock.json, frontend/.nvmrc. No lockfile is ignored.
#
# Pattern conventions used throughout:
#   /name/    anchored - matches only at the repository root
#   name/     matches a directory of that name at ANY depth (use sparingly)
#   name      matches a file, directory or symlink of that name at any depth
#   !name     re-inclusion. gitignore is LAST-MATCH-WINS, so every negation
#             must appear AFTER the patterns that would otherwise match it,
#             and git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
#             excluded - restructure the pattern rather than negating into one.
# ===========================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Python byte-code and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class

# Compiled C extensions - psycopg[binary] and greenlet ship or build these
*.so


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Python packaging output - ANCHORED ON PURPOSE. DO NOT DROP THE SLASHES.
#
# The deleted template listed these unanchored: `build/`, `dist/`, `lib/`,
# `lib64/`, `var/`, `target/` and friends. A pattern with a trailing slash but
# NO LEADING slash matches a directory of that name at any depth, so the
# template's `lib/` also matched `frontend/src/lib/` - silently untracking the
# frontend's entire API client, contract-type, validation and utility layer
# (frontend/src/lib/api/client.ts is the only module in the frontend that
# performs HTTP). The result is a repository that still builds for whoever ran
# it first and is unbuildable from a fresh clone, with nothing to see in
# `git status`. Anchoring preserves the original intent - a root-level Python
# build tree - without reaching into source directories.
#
# Never restore the unanchored form of any pattern in this section.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/dist/
/sdist/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/var/
/target/
/wheels/
.eggs/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.Python

# PyPI upload credentials
.pypirc

# Cython debug symbols
cython_debug/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Virtual environments
#
# The interpreter is pinned by backend/.python-version (3.14.7); the venv it
# creates lives at backend/.venv and is always local, never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Test and coverage artefacts
#    pytest + pytest-cov on the backend; vitest and playwright on the frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.hypothesis/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Type-checker and linter caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.eslintcache
.cache/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Node and package managers
#
# Lockfiles are deliberately NOT ignored. Reproducible installs require
# frontend/package-lock.json to be tracked, and the same reasoning applies to
# every Python lock format. The upstream template left these commented out;
# they stay that way. Do not uncomment any of them:
#   #package-lock.json   #yarn.lock     #pnpm-lock.yaml
#   #Pipfile.lock        #poetry.lock   #poetry.toml
#   #uv.lock             #pdm.lock      #pdm.toml
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Next.js build output
#
# next-env.d.ts is regenerated by `next dev` and `next build` on every run and
# is conventionally untracked even though tsconfig.json lists it in `include`.
# tsconfig.json sets "incremental": true, which emits *.tsbuildinfo.
# `frontend/build/` is tier-scoped rather than global, for the same reason
# section 2 is anchored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.swc/
.turbo/
.vercel
frontend/build/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Frontend test artefacts
#    playwright html/blob reporters and its browser cache; vitest coverage
#    output is already covered by `coverage/` in section 4
#
# `playwright/.cache/` contains a slash, and git anchors any pattern containing
# a slash to the directory holding this file - so it covers only a root-level
# playwright cache. playwright.config.ts lives in frontend/, so the tier-scoped
# line is the one that actually does the work here; both are listed so neither
# location depends on the broad `.cache/` in section 5 to catch it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
playwright-report/
blob-report/
test-results/
playwright/.cache/
frontend/playwright/.cache/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Environment files - THE SECRET BOUNDARY
#
# Real values (DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET_KEY, SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD and the rest)
# belong only in untracked files. `.env.example` is the ONLY environment file
# in version control and it carries placeholders exclusively.
#
# Because gitignore is last-match-wins, the `!.env.example` negation below
# MUST remain after the `.env.*` catch-all. Moving it earlier makes it a no-op
# and untracks the configuration contract the whole platform is documented by.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.production.local
.env.test.local
# Catch-all for any further per-environment file: .env.staging, .env.ci, ...
.env.*
# direnv
.envrc

# The committed contract, re-included LAST so the catch-all cannot untrack it.
!.env.example


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Editors and operating-system noise
#
# `.idea/` and `.vscode/` stay COMMENTED OUT on purpose - this project imposes
# no editor policy. Ignore them for yourself instead:
#   git config --global core.excludesFile ~/.gitignore_global
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#.idea/
# .vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# macOS and Windows
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Logs and local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
tmp/
.tmp/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 12. Local database artefacts and dumps
#
# PostgreSQL 18 is the mandated system of record and the product has no SQLite
# fallback anywhere. These patterns exist only so a developer's throwaway
# local database or a `pg_dump` output cannot be committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.db
*.dump
*.sql.gz


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 13. Automation artefacts
#
# Screenshots and screen recordings captured by tooling during validation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
blitzy/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 14. Deliberately tracked - safeguards, kept last so nothing overrides them
#
# backend/.python-version pins the interpreter at 3.14.7 and is this project's
# only Python version declaration, so it must stay in version control. The
# upstream template listed `.python-version` commented out, which suits a
# library that runs on many interpreters; this is a service pinned to exactly
# one. No `.python-version` pattern appears anywhere above, and the negation
# below is a belt-and-braces guard in case one is ever added.
#
# Also intentionally absent from this file, and required to stay tracked:
#   docs/**                      architecture.md, api/, features/ - never add
#                                a `docs/` or `docs/_build/` pattern here
#   .github/workflows/ci.yml     pipeline definition
#   .env.example                 environment contract (re-included in 9 above)
#   frontend/.nvmrc              Node 24.19.0 pin
#   frontend/package.json        dependency pins
#   frontend/package-lock.json   resolved dependency tree
#   backend/requirements.txt     runtime pins
#   backend/requirements-dev.txt development pins
#   backend/pyproject.toml       project metadata and tool configuration
#   backend/alembic.ini          migration configuration
#   frontend/public/*            favicon, icons and the default social card
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!backend/.python-version
